nodecode-modular is a rewrite of tommyjtl's tommyjtl/hermes-modular-provider:
https://github.com/tommyjtl/hermes-modular-provider
commit bfd4510df3cb2218300f3a059414ecbf8e479366
Apache-2.0 (LICENSE): the file is the stock Apache License 2.0 text and its
copyright line is left as the template it ships with, "Copyright [yyyy] [name of
copyright owner]"; the plugin's manifest declares the author as "Modular
(tommyjtl)"

Rewritten: the provider profile itself (its default base of
https://api.modular.com/v1, its MODULAR_API_KEY variable, its four-model
fallback list and its OpenAI-compatible chat wire) as a Nodecode catalog row
and one request-body hook; the model table, which sends each model the
window, modalities and reasoning ladder the original measured --
MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash with five levels, deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017
with three, minimax/minimax-m3 and google/gemma-4-31b-it with a toggle and
none; and the clamp that lowers a pick the model does not take to the nearest
weaker one, never raises it, and turns thinking off with the model's own switch
or, where nothing stops it, with its lightest level.

Added, because Nodecode's catalog is where a picker reads its list: the row
itself, since models.dev publishes no provider at Modular's address, so
without it the provider could be neither chosen nor dialled.

Left out, and why: the Hermes private seams the original imported
(providers.base, ProviderProfile, register_provider) have no place here, so the
profile is a catalog row and its two methods (fetch_models,
build_api_kwargs_extras) are the row's model table and one request-body hook;
its `GET /v1/models` read is not repeated, since the four models are the whole
list it kept; and its default auxiliary model has no per-provider equivalent
in Nodecode.
